# Optional: override GA4 ID (defaults to G-WFT80SQKPP in src/lib/gtag.ts)
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
# Without a key, PSI allows very few runs per day; each funnel snapshot calls PSI twice (mobile + desktop).
# Cloud Console: enable "PageSpeed Insights API", then create an API key under Credentials.
# PAGESPEED_API_KEY=your_google_api_key

# Resend — https://resend.com (create API key + verify sending domain or use onboarding domain for tests)
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Must match a verified sender in Resend (e.g. FlowXsell <reports@yourdomain.com>)
RESEND_FROM="FlowXsell <onboarding@resend.dev>"

# Raffle business-card gallery (Supabase: project URL + service role from Settings → API)
# 1) Run api/raffle-setup.sql in Supabase SQL Editor (once).
# 2) Storage → New bucket → name: raffle-cards → Public bucket ON.
# 3) Add these to Vercel (and local .env for npm run dev:full):
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...   # never expose in frontend or client bundles
# Optional: require header X-Raffle-Secret on POST /api/raffle-upload (server-to-server only; not for browsers)
# RAFFLE_UPLOAD_SECRET=
# Admin-only: POST /api/raffle-delete (header X-Raffle-Admin). Use a long random string; open raffle page once as ?admin=<key> to store in session.
# RAFFLE_ADMIN_KEY=

# ─── /analytics surface (Shopify Analytics & Landing Page Intelligence) ───────
#
# This Vite app’s /api/shopify-* routes read ONLY the three variables below.
# Storefront API tokens (public hex, or “private” tokens for /api/.../graphql.json
# on the STOREFRONT endpoint) are NOT read anywhere in this repo — keeping them
# in .env for your headless site or other tools is fine, but they will NOT power
# this dashboard until you add a separate Admin API token.
#
# Without SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN + SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN, /analytics uses Tuskegee
# mock data (isDemo). Restart `npm run dev:full` after any change here.
#
# How to get the Admin API token:
# 1) Shopify admin → Settings → Apps and sales channels → Develop apps → Create app
# 2) Configuration → Admin API access scopes: enable read_products, read_orders, read_reports
#    read_reports powers ShopifyQL session timeseries (Admin → Analytics–class data).
#    (Optional: read_all_orders if you need orders older than ~60 days for custom apps, e.g. 6–9 month charts.)
# 3) Install app → API credentials → copy the Admin API access token (starts with shpat_)
#
# Example: keep headless vars for other projects, add Admin for FlowXsell only:
#
#   # (optional — not used by this codebase; your Hydrogen/Next app may use these)
#   # VITE_PUBLIC_STORE_DOMAIN=
#   # PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN=
#
#   SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=your-lrt-store.myshopify.com
#   SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#   SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=2025-01
#
SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=your-store.myshopify.com
SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=2024-10

# Anthropic — powers POST /api/generate-landing-page (structured JSON + extended thinking).
# Create a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys — server / Vercel only, never VITE_*.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Optional: defaults to claude-sonnet-4-6 (must support structured outputs + thinking).
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# ─── Shopify Admin smoke test (no VITE_*; server / Vercel only) ─────────────────
# After `npm run dev:full`, verify credentials before /analytics:
#   curl -sS "http://localhost:3001/api/shopify-smoke" | jq .
# Production (replace host):
#   curl -sS "https://YOUR_DOMAIN/api/shopify-smoke" | jq .
# Expect HTTP 200 + ok:true + sampleProductTitle when read_products works.
# 401/403/404 meanings are echoed in JSON (see api/shopify-smoke.js).
